/**
 * @page api API Reference
 *
 * @section api_overview Overview
 * The ArgusAI API provides RESTful endpoints for object detection and segmentation.
 * All endpoints are prefixed with `/api/`.
 *
 * @section api_auth Authentication
 * Currently, the API does not require authentication. All endpoints are publicly accessible.
 *
 * @section api_endpoints Endpoints
 *
 * @subsection api_get_class_names GET /api/class-names
 * Returns the list of available object classes for detection.
 *
 * @code{.json}
 * Response:
 * {
 *   "class_names": [
 *     "person", "bicycle", "car", "motorcycle", "airplane",
 *     // ... more classes ...
 *   ]
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection api_detect POST /api/detect
 * Performs object detection or segmentation on an uploaded image.
 *
 * @code{.json}
 * Request:
 * Content-Type: multipart/form-data
 * {
 *   "file": <image_file>,
 *   "task": "detection" | "segmentation",
 *   "selected_classes": ["person", "car", ...],
 *   "threshold": 0.25,
 *   "show_labels": true,
 *   "show_confidence": true,
 *   "color": "#B9282B",
 *   "thickness": 2
 * }
 *
 * Response:
 * {
 *   "image": "<base64_encoded_image>",
 *   "format": "png",
 *   "message": "Detection completed successfully"
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section api_parameters Parameters
 *
 * @subsection api_file File
 * - Type: File upload
 * - Required: Yes
 * - Description: Image file to process
 * - Supported formats: JPG, PNG, JPEG
 *
 * @subsection api_task Task
 * - Type: String
 * - Required: Yes
 * - Values: "detection" | "segmentation"
 * - Description: Type of processing to perform
 *
 * @subsection api_selected_classes Selected Classes
 * - Type: Array of strings
 * - Required: No
 * - Description: List of object classes to detect
 * - Default: All classes
 *
 * @subsection api_threshold Threshold
 * - Type: Float
 * - Required: No
 * - Range: 0.0 to 1.0
 * - Default: 0.25
 * - Description: Confidence threshold for detections
 *
 * @subsection api_show_labels Show Labels
 * - Type: Boolean
 * - Required: No
 * - Default: true
 * - Description: Whether to show class labels on the output image
 *
 * @subsection api_show_confidence Show Confidence
 * - Type: Boolean
 * - Required: No
 * - Default: true
 * - Description: Whether to show confidence scores on the output image
 *
 * @subsection api_color Color
 * - Type: String
 * - Required: No
 * - Default: "#B9282B"
 * - Description: Color for bounding boxes and labels (HEX format)
 *
 * @subsection api_thickness Thickness
 * - Type: Integer
 * - Required: No
 * - Default: 2
 * - Description: Thickness of bounding boxes in pixels
 *
 * @section api_errors Error Responses
 * All endpoints may return the following error responses:
 *
 * @code{.json}
 * {
 *   "error": "Error message description"
 * }
 * @endcode
 *
 * Common error codes:
 * - 400: Bad Request - Invalid parameters
 * - 413: Payload Too Large - Image file too large
 * - 415: Unsupported Media Type - Invalid file format
 * - 500: Internal Server Error - Server-side processing error
 *
 * @section api_examples Examples
 *
 * @subsection api_example_curl cURL Example
 * @code{.bash}
 * curl -X POST "http://localhost:8000/api/detect" \
 *   -H "Content-Type: multipart/form-data" \
 *   -F "file=@image.jpg" \
 *   -F "task=detection" \
 *   -F "selected_classes=[\"person\",\"car\"]" \
 *   -F "threshold=0.25" \
 *   -F "show_labels=true" \
 *   -F "show_confidence=true" \
 *   -F "color=#B9282B" \
 *   -F "thickness=2"
 * @endcode
 *
 * @subsection api_example_python Python Example
 * @code{.python}
 * import requests
 *
 * url = "http://localhost:8000/api/detect"
 * files = {"file": open("image.jpg", "rb")}
 * data = {
 *     "task": "detection",
 *     "selected_classes": ["person", "car"],
 *     "threshold": 0.25,
 *     "show_labels": True,
 *     "show_confidence": True,
 *     "color": "#B9282B",
 *     "thickness": 2
 * }
 *
 * response = requests.post(url, files=files, data=data)
 * result = response.json()
 * @endcode
 */ 